.\" kettle.1 - manual page for kettle terminal emulator
.\" Format: man-pages macros. Render preview: `man -l packaging/linux/kettle.1`
.\" Render to text: `groff -man -Tutf8 packaging/linux/kettle.1 | less`
.TH KETTLE 1 "2026-05-21" "kettle" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
kettle \- fast, cross-platform, GPU-accelerated terminal emulator
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kettle
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ \-\-\ COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS... ]]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kettle
is a Rust-based terminal emulator combining the best ideas of
.BR Ghostty ,
.BR Terminator ,
.BR kitty ,
.B Alacritty
and
.B WezTerm
into one tool. Cross-platform (Linux, macOS, Windows), GPU-accelerated
via
.BR wgpu ,
and built on the battle-tested
.B alacritty_terminal
VT engine.
.PP
Features include split panes (Terminator-style binary tree),
multiple tabs with drag-to-reorder + activity / silence / bell
indicators, inline images (sixel, kitty graphics, iTerm2 inline
image protocols), OSC 8 hyperlinks, OSC 133 shell-integration
jump-to-prompt, ligatures, infinite scrollback, fuzzy-search
overlays (command palette, themes, SSH-host launcher), undo
close tab, duplicate tab/pane, and broadcast / group-input mode.
.PP
Without arguments
.B kettle
launches a windowed session running the user's default shell.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Launch
.TP
.BI \-e \ "PROGRAM \fR[\fIARGS...\fR]"
Run
.I PROGRAM
instead of the default shell. Everything after
.B \-e
is treated as the command and its arguments.
.TP
.BI \-\-working-directory \ "DIR" \fR,\fP\fB\ \-d\ \fIDIR
Set the initial working directory for the launched program.
Hard-fails with a non-zero exit status if
.I DIR
does not exist (catches typos at launch time, not at the first
.B cd
inside the running shell).
.TP
.BI \-\-config \ FILE
Load configuration from
.I FILE
instead of the auto-detected path. Hard-fails if the path doesn't exist.
.
.SS Introspection (prints and exits)
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version string (with the git SHA on git checkouts) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print every flag and its description.
.TP
.B \-\-config-path
Print the resolved config-file path (or the fallback message if no
config is loaded) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-check-config
Validate the resolved config and print every effective setting +
diagnostic lines for unknown keys / malformed values.
.TP
.B \-\-print-default-config
Print every option with its default value, in the Ghostty-style
.RI """ key " = " value """
format. Useful as a starting point for
.IR ~/.config/kettle/config .
.TP
.B \-\-gpu-info
Print the
.B wgpu
adapter / backend / driver / texture-limit details kettle would
use on this machine. Useful for "blank window" / "no GPU adapter"
bug reports.
.TP
.B \-\-list-themes
Print every bundled theme name (>500 themes, sourced from the
Ghostty + iTerm2-Color-Schemes sets).
.TP
.B \-\-list-actions
Print every recognized keybind action name + every alias.
.TP
.B \-\-list-keybinds
Print every active keybind (default + user-overridden), grouped
by trigger.
.TP
.B \-\-list-ssh-hosts
Print every
.BR ssh-host
declaration in the config + every freeform host kettle has cached
from prior
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
launcher use.
.TP
.BI \-\-shell-integration \ "SHELL"
Print the OSC 133 shell-integration snippet for
.I SHELL
(one of:
.BR bash ", " zsh ", " fish ).
Append to your rc file to enable jump-to-prompt
.RB ( "Ctrl+Up" " / " "Ctrl+Down" )
inside kettle:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
kettle --shell-integration bash >> ~/.bashrc
.EE
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-print-completions \ SHELL
Print a tab-completion script for the kettle CLI in
.IR SHELL 's
native format. Supports
.BR bash ", " zsh ", " fish ", " powershell ", "
and
.BR elvish .
.
.SS Debug / capture
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot \ PATH
Render one frame of the canonical kettle layout (single pane,
TokyoNight Night theme) to a PNG file at
.IR PATH .
Honors
.BR \-\-cols ", " \-\-rows ", and " \-\-config .
Used by the visual-regression CI smoke + the
.IR docs/PERFORMANCE.md
baseline.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot-menu \ PATH
Same as
.B \-\-screenshot
but renders with a synthetic right-click context menu open over
the pane. Useful for visually verifying the menu's render path
without an interactive window, and for pixel-level visual-
regression tests in CI.
.TP
.BI \-\-cols \ "N\fR, \fP\fB\-\-rows \ N"
Override the rendered grid size (in cells) for
.BR \-\-screenshot " / " \-\-screenshot-menu .
Default 96x28.
.TP
.BI \-\-tab\-handoff \ PATH
Restore a tab from a JSON handoff file written by another
.B kettle
process. Used by
.B Action::MoveTabToNewWindow
on platforms without SCM_RIGHTS (Windows + Wayland): the source
process serializes the focused tab + passes the path; the target
reads + reconstructs. Running shells stay in the source window —
live PTY-fd transfer needs
.BR \-\-tab\-handoff\-fd .
The handoff file is deleted after read (one-shot).
.TP
.BI \-\-tab\-handoff\-fd \ FD
Receive a tab handoff via SCM_RIGHTS over the named inherited
file descriptor. Used by
.B Action::MoveTabToNewWindow
on Linux + macOS where SCM_RIGHTS is available. Unix-only.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-send \ TEXT
Send
.I TEXT
to the running kettle's focused pane via the file-based IPC.
Cross-platform (no D-Bus needed). Pair with
.B \-\-remote\-file
to address a non-default kettle instance.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-file \ PATH
Override the IPC drop path used by
.B \-\-remote\-send " / " \-\-toggle .
Default is the per-user state dir; useful when running multiple
kettle instances each with their own remote-control endpoint.
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Show / hide the running kettle window (Yakuake / Tilda / Ghostty
quick-terminal parity). Bind a compositor / DE / OS
global hotkey to
.B kettle \-\-toggle
for one-key drop-down access.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile \ NAME
Launch with the named profile. Profiles live in the
config file as
.B profile = name=...
entries — argv-supplied profile overrides the default-startup one
without editing the config.
.TP
.BI \-\-layout \ NAME
Restore a named saved layout on startup. Layouts are stored
under
.IR ~/.config/kettle/layouts/ " ;"
see
.B Action::SaveLayoutAs " / " Action::RestoreLayout
for in-window save/restore.
.TP
.BI \-\-accent \ COLOR
Tint this window's chrome (peacock parity) with the
named or hex color, so multiple kettle windows are visually
distinct. Accepts
.B "#RRGGBB"
or any palette name from
.BR \-\-list\-themes .
.TP
.BI \-\-lua\-script \ PATH
Load
.I PATH
as the init script instead of the default
.IR ~/.config/kettle/init.lua .
The script runs in the
.B lua-sandbox = safe
sandbox by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-annotate \ TEXT
Overlay
.I TEXT
as a single caption along the bottom of the
.B \-\-screenshot
/
.B \-\-screenshot\-menu
output (iTerm2 "annotated screenshot" parity). A single non-repeatable bottom
caption \(em not a per-cell annotation.
.TP
.B \-\-write\-default\-config
Write the embedded default configuration to the resolved config path, creating
the parent directory, then exit. Refuses to overwrite an existing file. The
easiest cross-platform way to bootstrap a config \(em preferred over a shell
redirect on Windows PowerShell, whose
.B >
writes UTF-16.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-update
Check the GitHub releases API once for a newer kettle version, print the result,
and exit. Honors the
.B update\-check = false
opt-out and never runs on first launch.
.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
Defaults (every binding remappable via
.IR ~/.config/kettle/config 's
.B keybind
entries). Cmd is the macOS modifier; Ctrl on Linux / Windows.
.SS Tabs
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+T
new tab
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+W
close focused pane (or tab if last pane)
.TP
.B Ctrl+PgUp
previous tab
.TP
.B Ctrl+PgDn
next tab
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+PgUp
move tab left
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+PgDn
move tab right
.TP
.B Alt+1 ... Alt+9
jump to tab N by number
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+I
new window
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Q
close window
.TP
.B F11
toggle fullscreen
.SS Splits / panes
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+O
split top/bottom (Terminator-exact)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+E
split left/right (Terminator-exact)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+A
auto-split (longest axis)
.TP
.B Alt+arrow
focus pane up / down / left / right
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+N
focus next pane (DFS order)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
focus previous pane
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+X
toggle pane zoom (maximize / restore)
.PP
Additional actions available via the command palette
.RB ( Ctrl+Shift+K ):
.BR UndoCloseTab ,
.BR DuplicateTab ,
.BR DuplicatePane ,
.BR Reset
\(em not default-bound (bind via the
.B keybind
config entry if you want a hotkey).
.SS Overlays
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+K
command palette (fuzzy actions)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+F
find in scrollback (regex + smart-case)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+H
URL / path quick-select hints
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
SSH-host launcher
.SS Scrollback / clipboard
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
copy selection
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+V
paste (bracketed if app enabled it)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Up
jump to previous OSC 133 prompt
.TP
.B Ctrl+Down
jump to next OSC 133 prompt
.SS Scrollback movement
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down
scroll one line
.TP
.B PageUp/PageDown
scroll one page
.SS Vi-mode (Alacritty parity)
Enter vi-mode for the focused pane's scrollback. A magenta hollow
block marks the vi cursor; the terminal cursor stays in place so
you can see both. Movement, visual selection, and yank all live
on standard vi keys.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Space
toggle vi-mode (enter / exit)
.TP
.B h j k l
move vi cursor left / down / up / right
.TP
.B arrow keys
same as h/j/k/l
.TP
.B 0 ^
jump to line start
.TP
.B $
jump to line end
.TP
.B g H
jump to top of viewport
.TP
.B G L
jump to bottom of viewport
.TP
.B M
jump to middle of viewport
.TP
.B v
toggle char-visual selection (anchor at cursor)
.TP
.B y
yank visual selection to clipboard, exit vi-mode
.TP
.B Esc
exit vi-mode
.SS Quake / dropdown mode
.TP
.B kettle \-\-toggle
flip the running window's visibility, sent via the remote-control
IPC. Bind your compositor / DE / OS global hotkey to this for
Quake / Yakuake / Tilda dropdown UX.
.SS Group / broadcast
.TP
.B Super+G
toggle broadcast (group-input) on this tab
.TP
.B Shift+Super+G
turn broadcast off
.SS Font size
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Plus
increase font size
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Minus
decrease font size
.TP
.B Ctrl+0
reset font size to the configured default
.SS Pane resize
.TP
.B Shift+Arrow
resize the focused split (up / down / left / right). Composes
with split-tree weights so adjacent panes grow proportionally.
.SS Scroll
.TP
.B Shift+PgUp
.TQ
.B Shift+PgDn
scroll one page up / down through scrollback
.TP
.B Shift+Home
.TQ
.B Shift+End
jump to scrollback top / bottom
.SS Right-click
A right click anywhere in a pane opens a context menu with:
Copy / Paste / Split Right / Split Down / Close Pane / New Tab.
.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration lives at
.IR ~/.config/kettle/config
(Linux),
.IR ~/Library/Application\ Support/kettle/config
(macOS), or
.IR %APPDATA%\\kettle\\config
(Windows). Format is Ghostty-style
.RI """ key " = " value """
lines; everything after
.B #
is a comment.
.PP
See
.B kettle\ \-\-print\-default\-config
for every option with its default + inline docstring, and the
.B kettle
docs at
.UR https://github.com/Reddimus/kettle/blob/main/docs/CONFIG.md
.UE
for the full reference.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
Program kettle launches when no
.B \-e
is given.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Standard
.B env_logger
filter (e.g.
.IR info ", " debug ", " "kettle=trace" ).
Default
.I warn
surfaces session-restore failures + GPU init errors on stderr.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Linux/Unix config root (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.TP
.B KETTLE_VERSION " / " KETTLE_PREFIX
Used by
.B scripts/install-online.sh
(the curl-pipe installer), not the
.B kettle
binary itself.
.B KETTLE_VERSION
pins which release to download;
.B KETTLE_PREFIX
overrides the install root.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kettle/config
User config file (Linux). See CONFIGURATION above.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/kettle/sessions/
Per-window session JSON (atomic write-then-rename); restored on next
launch with the same window id. Failures are logged via
.BR log::warn! .
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/kettle
Default install location for the
.B scripts/install.sh
+
.B install-online.sh
paths.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/kettle.desktop
XDG launcher (GNOME Activities / KDE Krunner / rofi).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/kettle.svg
Scalable launcher icon (plus PNG fallbacks at 32 / 48 / 64 / 128 / 256).
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Launch a windowed kettle running
.BR htop :
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
kettle -e htop
.EE
.RE
.PP
Validate the resolved config and exit:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
kettle --check-config
.EE
.RE
.PP
Generate a fresh config file with every option commented:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
kettle --print-default-config > ~/.config/kettle/config
.EE
.RE
.PP
Diagnose a rendering bug (capture for issue report):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
kettle --gpu-info > /tmp/gpu.txt
kettle --screenshot /tmp/kettle.png
.EE
.RE
.
